section('summary','Executive summary',f'''<ul class="summary"><li><strong>Start with scoped integration prototypes.</strong> The stored readiness labels identify 1 likely-buildable and 65 constrained candidates out of 100. These are documentation inferences; no integration was executed.</li><li><strong>Auth support needs flexible credential handling.</strong> OAuth2 appears for 55/87 apps with auth evidence and API keys for 46/87; labels overlap and all 87 auth records are caveated. The other 13/100 are unresolved.</li><li><strong>Native MCP is a route to evaluate alongside APIs.</strong> Availability is recorded for 42/100 apps; 58/100 remain unresolved. Provider and ownership evidence have separate coverage, so a provider mention alone does not prove availability.</li><li><strong>Use evidence coverage to bound every decision.</strong> 45 source-backed, 798 caveated and 457 unresolved field dispositions out of 1,300. These are evidence states, not factual accuracy scores. Fresh purposive verification found errors and led to corrections.</li></ul><p class="note">Suggested action: use the candidate groups below to select one documented resource workflow, then confirm credentials, permissions, entitlement and operation behavior before promising a connector.</p>''')
